<title>UK: Angel Trains being readied for sale - newspaper.</title>
<headline>Angel Trains being readied for sale - newspaper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK rail leasing company Angel Trains is being prepared for sale or flotation, the Financial Times (FT) newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said U.S. bank Morgan Stanley was chosen to handle the sale of the business, which was sold by the government two years ago to a management team backed by Japanese securities house Nomura.</p>
<p>Analysts believe flotation could value the business at some one billion pounds ($1.6 billion), the FT said.</p>
<p>($ = 0.622 British Pounds)</p>
